  <regions type="content">
    <region left="0" top="0" width="429" height="56" color="#000000" fontSize="32">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="32">
        <content>
          <p>P3A Amplifier Design:</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="72" width="620" height="38" color="#000000" bgColor="#80ff80" fontSize="20">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="20">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #80ff80;">Section A: Voltage Rails and Power Considerations</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="126" width="709" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>The amplifier will be contructed as a BTL. Thus we want 40WattRMS into a 4Ω load.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="171" width="129" height="34" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">P.RMS</e>
          <e type="operand">90</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">watt</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="153" top="171" width="95" height="34" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">R.L</e>
          <e type="operand">8</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">ohm</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="270" top="171" width="107" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">V.cc</e>
          <e type="operand">33</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="405" top="180" width="124" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">V.ee</e>
          <e type="operand">33</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="1">-</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="207" width="278" height="56" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">V.peak</e>
          <e type="operand">2</e>
          <e type="operand">P.RMS</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operand">R.L</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="function" args="1">sqrt</e>
          <e type="operand">2</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">18.9737</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="252" width="233" height="61" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">I.peak</e>
          <e type="operand">2</e>
          <e type="operand">V.peak</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operand">R.L</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">4.7434</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">A</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="9" top="315" width="645" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="12">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 14px;">Therefore a power rail of +-25V should safely be able to power this amplifier.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="9" top="351" width="477" height="38" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="20">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 20px; background-color: #ffff80;">Section B: Choosing Closed Loop Gain</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="9" top="405" width="668" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>We expect a voltage of +-1Vrms into the power amplifier (after equalisation etc)</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="9" top="432" width="490" height="50" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>Resistors R5 and R4, part of the LTP, are responsible for <br />closed loop voltage gain.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="522" top="432" width="217" height="178" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="9" top="486" width="522" height="71" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>Based off of our desired Vpeak and the expected input <br />voltage, we can calculate the gain and therefore the resistors <br />use.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="9" top="567" width="248" height="63" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">V.rms</e>
          <e type="operand">V.peak</e>
          <e type="operand">2</e>
          <e type="function" args="1">sqrt</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">13.4164</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="261" top="567" width="221" height="61" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">A.v</e>
          <e type="operand">V.rms</e>
          <e type="operand">1</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">13.4164</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="9" top="639" width="668" height="71" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>I Choose a 100kOhm resistor as the Resistor R5, as that is what is available in <br />the labs. Therefore a resistor 7.45kOhm or smaller is a suitable choice for this <br />application</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="9" top="729" width="634" height="38" color="#000000" bgColor="#ff8080" fontSize="20">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="20">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ff8080;">Section C: Designing Wilson Current Source for LTP</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="558" top="783" width="174" height="210" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="27" top="792" width="560" height="91" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>The gain for the BC546B is about \[REGION[a453b255ec52490ab3e965f1af4440ef]]\ at a worst case <br />scenario when \[REGION[13ff85737b6244398e403e6c6478e18a]]\. We assume \[REGION[f9176ba3375a48478ea2b22362af5b78]]\ and<br />calculated on paper, I.O is equal to Iref. </p>
        </content>
        <regions>
          <region id="a453b255ec52490ab3e965f1af4440ef" left="283" top="0" width="136" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
            <math>
              <input>
                <e type="operand">h.fe.546</e>
                <e type="operand">200</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
              </input>
            </math>
          </region>
          <region id="13ff85737b6244398e403e6c6478e18a" left="128" top="31" width="120" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
            <math>
              <input>
                <e type="operand">I.O</e>
                <e type="operand">2.4</e>
                <e type="operand" style="unit">mA</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
              </input>
            </math>
          </region>
          <region id="f9176ba3375a48478ea2b22362af5b78" left="355" top="31" width="118" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
            <math>
              <input>
                <e type="operand">V.be</e>
                <e type="operand">1.4</e>
                <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
              </input>
            </math>
          </region>
        </regions>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="9" top="900" width="369" height="69" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">R.7</e>
          <e type="operand">V.cc</e>
          <e type="operand">V.ee</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
          <e type="operand">1.4</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
          <e type="operand">I.O</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">26916.6667</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">Ω</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="27" top="1071" width="423" height="38" color="#000000" bgColor="#ff80ff" fontSize="20">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p style="font-weight: normal; font-size: 20px; background-color: #ff80ff;">Designing Resistors R11 and R12:</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="594" top="1080" width="140" height="220" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="1125" width="546" height="71" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>Voltage drop in R12 should be about 1V. Therefore, using a <br />current of about 3.7mA, we get that the resistor should be about <br />270Ohm.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="27" top="1224" width="396" height="38" color="#000000" bgColor="#ff0080" fontSize="20">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="20">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ff0080;">Designing the boostrap network:</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="1287" width="392" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>The current into the bootstrap network will be:</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="558" top="1314" width="178" height="199" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="36" top="1332" width="143" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">h.fe.BD140</e>
          <e type="operand">40</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="207" top="1332" width="125" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">h.fe.35C</e>
          <e type="operand">25</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="27" top="1359" width="394" height="69" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">I.boot</e>
          <e type="operand">2</e>
          <e type="operand">I.peak</e>
          <e type="operand">h.fe.35C</e>
          <e type="operand">h.fe.BD140</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">mA</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">9.4868</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="36" top="1440" width="521" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>Therefore the resistors can be calculated from a voltage loop:</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="36" top="1485" width="308" height="69" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">R.boot</e>
          <e type="operand">V.peak</e>
          <e type="operand">V.ee</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
          <e type="operand">I.boot</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">kΩ</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">5.4785</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="36" top="1557" width="641" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="14">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="14">
        <content>
          <p>From simulations, I found that 1.6kΩ resistors match this value much closer.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
  </regions>
</worksheet>